{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789155264,"nonce":"dUxsfdJ9Oh7qeUCzViI0/qqPsFk=","title":"`cast this : Self` inside an enum abstract loses the underlying value","message":"Three symptoms, one construct. `/tmp/probe/SWABS2.hx`:\n\n    enum abstract Kind(Int) {\n        var A = 0; var B = 1; var C = 2;\n        public function viaCast():String {\n            return switch (cast this : Kind) { case A:\"a\"; case B:\"b\"; case C:\"c\"; };\n        }\n        public function viaThis():String {\n            return switch (this) { case 0:\"a\"; case 1:\"b\"; case _:\"c\"; };\n        }\n        public function viaLocal():String {\n            var k:Kind = cast this;\n            return switch (k) { case A:\"a\"; case B:\"b\"; case C:\"c\"; };\n        }\n        public function viaLocalResult():String {\n            var s = switch (cast this : Kind) { case A:\"a\"; case B:\"b\"; case C:\"c\"; };\n            return s;\n        }\n    }\n\nWith `var k:Kind = B` (underlying 1):\n\n| call | got | want |\n|---|---|---|\n| `k.viaCast()` | `\"\"` (empty) | `\"b\"` |\n| `k.viaThis()` | `\"b\"` | ok -- switching on `this` directly WORKS |\n| `k.viaLocal()` | `\"a\"` | `\"b\"` -- WRONG CASE, reads as 0 |\n| `k.viaLocalResult()` | SIGSEGV fault=0x1 | `\"b\"` |\n\n`this` inside an abstract IS the underlying value, so `cast this : Kind` should\nbe the identity. It is not: the value reads back as 0/absent, and in the last\nform the raw underlying 1 is dereferenced as a pointer.\n\n`viaThis` working is the discriminator -- the switch machinery is fine; the\n`cast this` is what loses the value.\n\nCORPUS IMPACT: this is `Xml.toString` (compiler/haxe-std/Xml.hx:64, the\n`XmlType` enum abstract), which the backend reports as\n\n    W0020 cannot compile `Xml.toString`\n    reason: Function 'toString' has return type String but encountered Return\n            with no value.\n\nand then trap-stubs. It appears in Issue11883 (WRONG_ANSWER), Issue4094\n(CRASH) and TestXML (CRASH).\n\n\"Return with no value\" is the single largest codegen-failure signature in the\ncorpus (12 occurrences across 11 tests); this accounts for 3 of them. The\nothers -- Issue2622 `return test(v)` through a function-typed parameter, and\nIssue10030 `return args.toArray()` on rest args -- are the same SHAPE\n(`return \u003cexpr\u003e` lowering to a valueless Return) but need their own check.","files":null}]}